<h2>A grid is rows in a col</h2>

<p>
  Put <c><row></c>s one under the other and every row is a line of equal parts. <c>size=</c> makes a part wider,
  <c>halign</c> and <c>valign</c> align inside it.
</p>

<row>
  <col>
    <h3>One</h3>

    <p>Plain text.</p>
  </col>
  <col>
    <h3>Two</h3>
    <code lang=python>
      <frame>
        x = 1
      </frame>
      <frame>
        x = 2   # on the first click
      </frame>
    </code>
  </col>
  <col>
    <h3>Three</h3>

    <p>Nothing special.</p>
  </col>
</row>

<row>
  <col halign=end>
    <h3>Four</h3>

    <p>Right-aligned with <c>halign=end</c>.</p>
  </col>
  <col size=2>
    <h3>Five (<c>size=2</c>)</h3>

    <p>This part is twice as wide as a normal one.</p>
  </col>
</row>
